    description: "The two CI pip-audit ignores treated as permanent, CVE-2025-71176 (pytest TOCTOU) and CVE-2026-3219 (pip archive confusion), matched nothing in the two audit environments rebuilt on 2026-09-27 for WI-totak (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/totak_09272026/{ci,rel}_noign.json). There, an audit with NO ignores exits 0: pytest resolves to 9.0.3 (core[dev] pins pytest~=9.0.2; the syrupy <9 cap that motivated the ignore no longer holds it back) and pip to 26.2.1. Both exit plans in ci.yml's comments are met in those envs.\n\nNOT CHECKED: the self-hosted runner's actual audit env (setup-python toolcache, which can carry packages from other jobs). That is the env the ignores protect, so it is the one to measure.\n\nTo do: drop both ids from the four lists (tests/test_audit_ignore_lists.py keeps them in step) and let the PR's own CI audit job be the measurement; if it fails, the failure names what the runner still carries."  # 9fa0
